  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#year">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Year position in a calendar-clock system.

The range of this property is not specified, so can be replaced by any specific representation of a calendar year from any calendar. </rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="es">Posición de año en un sistema calendario-reloj.

l rango de esta propiedad no está especificado, por tanto, se puede reemplazar por cualquier representación específica de un año de calendario de un calendario cualquiera.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#GeneralDateTimeDescription"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">year</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Sortal">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#EndurantType"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:EndurantType which carries (or supplies) a principle of identity for its instances  (see Guizzardi, 2005, chapter 4).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Sortal</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/def/propaphen#Phenomenon">
    <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">It is based on the meaning of the Propagation Phenomenon presented by "Król, Dariusz, Damien Fay, et Bogdan Gabryś, éd. Propagation Phenomena in Real World Networks. Vol. 85. Intelligent Systems Reference Library. Cham: Springer International Publishing, 2015. https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-15916-4."
        A phenomenon is a gufo:Perdurant that defines a fact or event of scientific interest susceptible to scientific description and explanation (Merriam-Webster dictionary). It does not define the occurrence of a phenomenon but the study of a type of it (i.e., Epidemic phenomena such as COVID-19, Influenza, etc.). As the mentioned phenomena, the study of a phenomenon may only be valid from the first occurrence of it until the last occurrence of it.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Nd31a72a89a5647ea94d100df06cdc96c"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>Propagation Phenomenon Type</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
